Two fixes to daslang's LLVM JIT (modules/dasLLVM/daslib), found while running
the wasm3 port under `daslang -jit` on the pinned commit 1524b3bf62e7decbfe530dc5f2e794b296fa1e68.
Applied in the local worktree tmp/daslang-jit; candidates for an upstream
pull request against GaijinEntertainment/daScript.

1. `reinterpret<uint64>(@@fn)` emitted an invalid bitcast from the function
   aggregate `{ ptr }` to i64 and aborted codegen (hit by op_Compile in the
   port). The pointer is extracted from the aggregate and converted with
   ptrtoint, which is the value the interpreter yields for the same cast.
2. A module-qualified builtin call (`math::sqrt`) reached the float-op1
   intrinsic emitter with the qualified spelling, producing the intrinsic name
   "llvm.math::sqrt.f32"; LLVMLookupIntrinsicID answers 0 and
   LLVMGetIntrinsicDeclaration dereferences it (SIGSEGV during codegen, hit by
   op_f32_Sqrt and the whole float_op1 family). The namespace is stripped and
   id 0 is refused with a diagnostic.

diff --git a/modules/dasLLVM/daslib/llvm_jit.das b/modules/dasLLVM/daslib/llvm_jit.das
index 14595cf8c..a27d34cec 100644
--- a/modules/dasLLVM/daslib/llvm_jit.das
+++ b/modules/dasLLVM/daslib/llvm_jit.das
@@ -5495,6 +5495,16 @@ class public LlvmJitVisitor : AstVisitor {
             res = LLVMBuildPtrToInt(g_builder, subE, type_to_llvm_type(ect), "cast_p_i")
         } elif ((ect.isPointer || ect.isString) && subT.isInteger) {
             res = LLVMBuildIntToPtr(g_builder, subE, type_to_llvm_type(ect), "cast_i_p")
+        } elif (subT.baseType == Type.tFunction && ect.isInteger &&
+                (ect.baseType == Type.tInt64 || ect.baseType == Type.tUInt64)) {
+            // A function value is the aggregate { ptr } (g_t_function), and LLVM
+            // rejects a bitcast from an aggregate to a scalar, so
+            // `reinterpret<uint64>(@@fn)` used to emit invalid IR
+            // ("Invalid bitcast %cast_r = bitcast { ptr } %x to i64") and abort
+            // codegen. Take the pointer out of the aggregate and convert that,
+            // which is the address the interpreter yields for the same cast.
+            var fn_ptr = LLVMBuildExtractValue(g_builder, subE, 0u, "cast_fn_p")
+            res = LLVMBuildPtrToInt(g_builder, fn_ptr, type_to_llvm_type(ect), "cast_fn_i")
         } elif (!ect.isRefType && !subT.isRefType) {
             if (ect.sizeOf == subT.sizeOf) {
                 res = LLVMBuildBitCast(g_builder, subE, type_to_llvm_type(ect), "cast_r")
